==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=welfare}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|welfare|lang=enm}}, probably from the {{etyl|ang|en}} phrase {{term|wel faran||to fare well, get along successfully, prosper|lang=ang}}  (cognate with {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|wolvare||welfare|lang=gml}}, Old Norse {{term|velferð|lang=non}}, Swedish {{term|välfärd|lang=sv}} and Dutch {{term|welvaart|lang=nl}}.) Equivalent to {{compound|well|fare}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈwɛlˌfɛə/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/"wEl%fE@/}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈwɛlˌfɛɚ/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/"wEl%fE@`/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} [[health|Health]], [[safety]], [[happiness]] and [[prosperity]]; [[well-being]] in any respect.
# {{context|uncountable|chiefly|US|lang=en}} Various forms of [[financial]] aid provided by the [[government]] to those who are in need of it (abbreviated form of ''Welfare assistance'').

====Synonyms====
* [[income support]], [[public assistance]], [[social security]] 

====Antonyms====
* [[illfare]]
* [[wofare]]

